WEBVTT

00:00:02.102 --> 00:00:06.266
Captain's Log, Stardate 48579.4.

00:00:06.306 --> 00:00:07.898
The crew has been
scanning constantly

00:00:07.941 --> 00:00:10.876
for anomalies that might help us
shorten our journey home.

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:13.708
Ensign Kim has reported
an exciting discovery...

00:00:13.747 --> 00:00:16.375
a subspace disturbance
which may be a wormhole.

00:00:16.416 --> 00:00:18.884
Let's see what you have,
Mr. Kim.

00:00:18.918 --> 00:00:21.318
There. It's registering
only on subspace bands.

00:00:21.354 --> 00:00:23.481
We don't even have it
on long-range sensors yet.

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:25.923
Verteron emanations.

00:00:25.959 --> 00:00:28.553
Tunneling secondary particles.

00:00:28.595 --> 00:00:30.995
It certainly looks
like a wormhole.

00:00:31.031 --> 00:00:32.362
But is it stable enough
for us to enter,

00:00:32.399 --> 00:00:33.991
and if it is,
where does it lead?

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:34.998
There is, of course,

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:37.001
a 75 percent chance
that a wormhole

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:38.799
will not lead
to the Alpha Quadrant.

00:00:38.838 --> 00:00:40.999
Very true, but you can also say

00:00:41.041 --> 00:00:42.804
there's a one in four chance
it will.

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:43.934
Those aren't bad odds.

00:00:43.977 --> 00:00:46.775
Any analysis yet, Ensign?

00:00:46.813 --> 00:00:47.780
Too far away.

00:00:47.814 --> 00:00:49.509
We'd have to be within
1,000 kilometers

00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:50.709
to get a detailed analysis,

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:53.878
but that would mean
a significant course change.

00:00:56.122 --> 00:00:58.022
Well, Mr. Kim,

00:00:58.124 --> 00:01:01.252
if there's even the possibility
of finding a wormhole,

00:01:01.294 --> 00:01:04.627
I think we can afford a detour.

00:01:04.664 --> 00:01:06.655
Lieutenant...

00:01:06.699 --> 00:01:10.157
input the coordinates
and change course.

00:01:10.203 --> 00:01:11.898
Aye, Captain.

00:01:11.938 --> 00:01:14.736
And may I suggest,
if this works,

00:01:14.774 --> 00:01:17.174
we petition the Federation
Astronomical Committee

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:21.772
to officially designate this
"The Harry Kim Wormhole."

00:03:18.129 --> 00:03:21.360
Captain, we're approaching
the coordinates of the wormhole.

00:03:21.399 --> 00:03:23.060
On screen.

00:03:24.602 --> 00:03:26.570
Are we in visual range?

00:03:26.604 --> 00:03:28.469
Affirmative, Captain,
and the anomaly is

00:03:28.506 --> 00:03:30.633
still registering
on subspace bands.

00:03:30.674 --> 00:03:33.643
Sensors also indicate
it's there.

00:03:33.677 --> 00:03:34.837
Magnify.

00:03:37.181 --> 00:03:39.411
Increase
to highest magnification.

00:03:44.455 --> 00:03:45.888
If that's a wormhole,
it must be

00:03:45.923 --> 00:03:47.413
the smallest one on record.

00:03:47.458 --> 00:03:50.325
Mr. Kim,
are you able to analyze it?

00:03:50.361 --> 00:03:52.693
Aye, Captain.
It's virtually microscopic.

00:03:52.730 --> 00:03:55.824
The aperture is only about
30 centimeters in diameter.

00:03:59.103 --> 00:04:02.971
I guess it's a little too small
for us to fly through.

00:04:06.944 --> 00:04:09.936
However... it might
be large enough

00:04:09.980 --> 00:04:11.948
to act as a conduit
for a message.

00:04:11.982 --> 00:04:13.347
That's right.

00:04:13.384 --> 00:04:15.352
It could carry
a compressed data transmission

00:04:15.386 --> 00:04:16.785
to Federation space in minutes.

00:04:16.821 --> 00:04:18.152
We still have to find out

00:04:18.189 --> 00:04:20.453
if it goes anywhere
near the Alpha Quadrant.

00:04:20.491 --> 00:04:22.618
Can you trace
its subspace bearing?

00:04:22.660 --> 00:04:25.288
I can't get any directional
readings at all.

00:04:25.329 --> 00:04:27.092
The aperture is too small.

00:04:27.131 --> 00:04:29.622
I recommend
we launch a microprobe

00:04:29.667 --> 00:04:31.294
into the wormhole.

00:04:31.335 --> 00:04:33.326
Agreed.
Do it, Lieutenant.

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:34.860
Aye, Captain.

00:04:37.908 --> 00:04:39.876
We're receiving telemetry.

00:04:50.721 --> 00:04:51.949
It doesn't look

00:04:51.989 --> 00:04:53.752
like any wormhole
I've ever studied.

00:04:53.791 --> 00:04:56.555
Microscopic gravitational
eddies,

00:04:56.594 --> 00:04:59.392
extremely constricted
spatial dimensions...

00:04:59.430 --> 00:05:02.763
The pathway is barely wider
than the probe itself.

00:05:02.800 --> 00:05:04.927
I think what we're seeing

00:05:05.002 --> 00:05:07.562
is a wormhole
in an advanced state of decay.

00:05:07.605 --> 00:05:09.266
It must be ancient.

00:05:09.306 --> 00:05:11.638
Probably been collapsing
for centuries.

00:05:11.675 --> 00:05:13.734
Does that mean we can't
send a message through it?

00:05:13.777 --> 00:05:15.301
No, I can do it.

00:05:15.346 --> 00:05:17.371
Maybe it'll take longer
to get through,

00:05:17.414 --> 00:05:19.143
but the wormhole's still
stable enough to carry

00:05:19.183 --> 00:05:20.343
a transmission.

00:05:20.384 --> 00:05:22.113
Any idea yet where that message
would end up, Ensign?

00:05:22.153 --> 00:05:25.088
I'll try extrapolating
the verteron exit vector.

00:05:26.757 --> 00:05:28.816
No, I can't get it.

00:05:28.859 --> 00:05:31.885
There's a strange phase variance
in the radiation stream.

00:05:31.929 --> 00:05:34.261
We'll have to wait
until the probe exits.

00:05:34.298 --> 00:05:36.266
That shouldn't take long.

00:05:39.303 --> 00:05:42.704
Captain, I'm getting
a distorted energy reading.

00:05:42.740 --> 00:05:45.903
The probe's telemetry
has changed.

00:05:49.947 --> 00:05:51.380
It's stuck.

00:05:51.415 --> 00:05:53.349
Stuck?

00:05:53.384 --> 00:05:54.976
It's mired
in a gravitational eddy,

00:05:55.085 --> 00:05:56.916
and because the wormhole's
in a state of collapse,

00:05:56.954 --> 00:05:59.684
those eddies are
incredibly dense.

00:06:02.459 --> 00:06:04.927
That probe
will never break free, Captain,

00:06:04.962 --> 00:06:06.930
and we'll have no way
of finding out

00:06:07.031 --> 00:06:08.464
where the wormhole ends.

00:06:08.499 --> 00:06:10.467
Let's give it some time.

00:06:10.501 --> 00:06:12.435
Maybe it will work itself loose.

00:06:17.975 --> 00:06:18.942
Captain.

00:06:19.043 --> 00:06:22.410
What is it, Ensign?

00:06:22.446 --> 00:06:23.936
Our probe...

00:06:24.014 --> 00:06:25.379
was just scanned.

00:06:25.416 --> 00:06:27.316
There's...

00:06:27.351 --> 00:06:30.616
there's somebody on
the other side of the wormhole.

00:06:36.860 --> 00:06:39.420
It started acting up
a couple of days ago.

00:06:39.463 --> 00:06:40.623
I've been working out
in the gym.

00:06:40.664 --> 00:06:42.222
Maybe I overdid it.

00:06:42.266 --> 00:06:43.290
Is it sore here?

00:06:43.334 --> 00:06:44.460
Yes.

00:06:44.501 --> 00:06:47.197
Localized tenderness
to the ulnar bone,

00:06:47.238 --> 00:06:49.968
no epidermal damage,
moderate edema.

00:06:50.074 --> 00:06:51.666
What are the possible diagnoses?

00:06:53.744 --> 00:06:56.577
Epicondylitis,
strained ligament,

00:06:56.614 --> 00:07:00.983
torn muscle,
and hairline fracture.

00:07:01.018 --> 00:07:02.542
That's exactly right.

00:07:02.586 --> 00:07:04.053
I've studied all the material
you gave me.

00:07:04.088 --> 00:07:05.112
I'm ready for more.

00:07:05.155 --> 00:07:06.452
Good.

00:07:06.490 --> 00:07:09.220
There's a great deal
more for you to learn.

00:07:09.260 --> 00:07:12.821
The tricorder indicates
this is a small stress fracture.

00:07:14.498 --> 00:07:16.932
Can this guy do everything
a real doctor does?

00:07:16.967 --> 00:07:18.628
Yes, he can.

00:07:18.669 --> 00:07:23.265
Activate it,
and direct the beam here.

00:07:25.242 --> 00:07:26.937
That's it.

00:07:27.011 --> 00:07:29.138
Not quite so fast.

00:07:29.179 --> 00:07:31.238
If I had to get treatment
for something serious...

00:07:31.282 --> 00:07:33.307
if I needed surgery,
for instance...

00:07:33.350 --> 00:07:35.045
would he be performing it?

00:07:35.085 --> 00:07:37.383
Of course,
and quite expertly, too.

00:07:37.421 --> 00:07:39.286
I don't know.

00:07:39.323 --> 00:07:41.120
I'd have to think twice
about that.

00:07:41.158 --> 00:07:43.490
Fine. And if you were lucky,
you wouldn't die on the table

00:07:43.527 --> 00:07:44.960
while you were
making up your mind.

00:07:44.995 --> 00:07:45.962
That should do it.

00:07:45.996 --> 00:07:46.963
How does it feel?

00:07:47.031 --> 00:07:48.430
Not bad.

00:07:50.134 --> 00:07:51.726
Thanks.

00:08:00.144 --> 00:08:02.169
Doctor, did you notice

00:08:02.212 --> 00:08:04.180
how rudely that officer
treated you?

00:08:04.214 --> 00:08:05.772
No more so than most.

00:08:05.816 --> 00:08:07.875
You mean others act that way,
too?

00:08:07.918 --> 00:08:09.783
Let's just say,
I've become accustomed

00:08:09.820 --> 00:08:11.515
to being treated
like a hypospray.

00:08:13.624 --> 00:08:16.787
Now, here's some material
on first aid for burns.

00:08:16.827 --> 00:08:18.818
Doctor, I think
I'd like to do more

00:08:18.862 --> 00:08:20.090
than study first aid.

00:08:20.130 --> 00:08:21.859
I'd be interested
in knowing more

00:08:21.899 --> 00:08:23.867
about anatomy and physiology.

00:08:23.901 --> 00:08:25.766
You're intellectually curious.

00:08:25.803 --> 00:08:27.668
I like that.

00:08:32.509 --> 00:08:34.204
These deal with human anatomy

00:08:34.244 --> 00:08:36.872
and physiology, but they weren't
written for the layman.

00:08:36.914 --> 00:08:38.472
They're quite technical.

00:08:38.515 --> 00:08:39.846
I understand.

00:08:39.883 --> 00:08:41.282
I'll do my best.

00:08:41.318 --> 00:08:43.843
And I really
appreciate your help.

00:08:49.593 --> 00:08:51.891
We've analyzed the data.

00:08:51.929 --> 00:08:53.521
So far, our sensors
have detected

00:08:53.564 --> 00:08:55.691
four separate scans
of the microprobe...

00:08:55.732 --> 00:08:57.927
each one on a progressively
narrower band.

00:08:57.968 --> 00:08:59.765
Someone on the other end
of that wormhole

00:08:59.803 --> 00:09:01.395
is definitely interested
in that probe.

00:09:01.438 --> 00:09:03.702
We cannot preclude
the possibility that there is

00:09:03.740 --> 00:09:05.469
a microscopic entity
within the wormhole,

00:09:05.509 --> 00:09:07.909
curious about an intruder.

00:09:07.945 --> 00:09:10.038
That's possible,
but you'd think our probe

00:09:10.080 --> 00:09:11.240
would have detected
something like that.

00:09:11.281 --> 00:09:13.841
What's the condition
of the probe now?

00:09:13.884 --> 00:09:16.079
I've been monitoring it
from Engineering.

00:09:16.119 --> 00:09:19.054
It's still embedded
in the gravitational eddy,

00:09:19.089 --> 00:09:21.717
but within 72 hours,
it will be crushed.

00:09:21.758 --> 00:09:22.782
But until then,

00:09:22.826 --> 00:09:25.226
it should continue
to transmit telemetry.

00:09:25.262 --> 00:09:27.025
If we're reading scans
from the other side,

00:09:27.064 --> 00:09:29.658
it's possible the probe
is acting as a relay.

00:09:29.700 --> 00:09:31.861
If that's true,
we should be able to use it

00:09:31.902 --> 00:09:33.062
to transmit a message

00:09:33.103 --> 00:09:34.934
to whoever is executing
the scan.

00:09:34.972 --> 00:09:38.464
Yes. I can modify our
subspace communications band

00:09:38.509 --> 00:09:40.704
to accept the probe
as a booster.

00:09:40.744 --> 00:09:42.609
Let's try it, Mr. Kim.

00:09:42.646 --> 00:09:44.637
I'll give you a hand.

00:09:48.118 --> 00:09:50.086
I fear Mr. Kim's exuberance

00:09:50.120 --> 00:09:52.350
may turn into an equally
intense disappointment

00:09:52.389 --> 00:09:54.186
if his efforts prove in vain.

00:09:54.224 --> 00:09:56.852
You may be right,
but I'd rather assume

00:09:56.894 --> 00:09:58.691
that he's going
to be successful.

00:10:03.600 --> 00:10:07.092
Okay, I've boosted power
to the communications bandwidth.

00:10:07.137 --> 00:10:08.365
Now, all we have to do

00:10:08.405 --> 00:10:09.963
is reconfigure
the signal generator

00:10:10.073 --> 00:10:12.564
so it's compatible with
the probe's long-range sensors.

00:10:12.609 --> 00:10:13.701
I'm on it.

00:10:13.744 --> 00:10:15.871
Just a few minutes more.

00:10:15.913 --> 00:10:17.380
This has to work.

00:10:17.414 --> 00:10:19.075
It'll mean so much
to people back home

00:10:19.116 --> 00:10:22.483
to know we're alive
and headed for Federation space.

00:10:22.519 --> 00:10:24.612
We haven't been gone that long.

00:10:24.655 --> 00:10:26.646
People won't give up on us
so soon.

00:10:26.690 --> 00:10:28.749
They probably just think
we're lost.

00:10:31.061 --> 00:10:33.359
It's still going
to be hard on my folks.

00:10:33.397 --> 00:10:35.365
I always called them
once a week,

00:10:35.399 --> 00:10:38.630
even when I was
on my training missions.

00:10:38.669 --> 00:10:41.797
I've never been out of contact
for so long.

00:10:43.707 --> 00:10:46.175
Well, it is going to work,
Starfleet,

00:10:46.209 --> 00:10:48.109
so pretty soon they're going
to know you're all right.

00:10:51.381 --> 00:10:53.349
How about you?

00:10:53.383 --> 00:10:55.112
Any family?

00:10:56.954 --> 00:10:59.013
I haven't seen my father
since I was five.

00:10:59.089 --> 00:11:00.716
He and my mother separated.

00:11:00.757 --> 00:11:02.122
He went back to Earth,

00:11:02.159 --> 00:11:04.627
and, um, that was
the last I saw of him.

00:11:06.396 --> 00:11:07.693
And your mom?

00:11:07.731 --> 00:11:11.223
I think
she's on the Klingon Homeworld.

00:11:11.268 --> 00:11:12.428
You think?

00:11:12.469 --> 00:11:14.596
We didn't get along very well.

00:11:15.872 --> 00:11:17.169
Okay.

00:11:17.207 --> 00:11:18.697
The signal generator
should be tuned

00:11:18.742 --> 00:11:20.334
to the probe's
long-range sensors.

00:11:20.377 --> 00:11:24.211
Isn't there anyone back home
who'd be worried about you?

00:11:24.247 --> 00:11:27.114
The Maquis are as close
to family as I've ever had.

00:11:27.150 --> 00:11:30.950
Most of my friends
are here on the ship,

00:11:30.988 --> 00:11:34.082
so... no.

00:11:34.124 --> 00:11:36.592
There's no one back home
who's going to care

00:11:36.627 --> 00:11:38.993
one way or another
whether I'm alive.

00:11:40.163 --> 00:11:42.097
We're ready to transmit.

00:11:42.132 --> 00:11:44.464
Engineering to Bridge.

00:11:44.501 --> 00:11:45.695
Janeway here.

00:11:45.736 --> 00:11:48.762
We have a communications link
with the microprobe.

00:11:48.805 --> 00:11:51.672
We're going to try sending
a preliminary test signal...

00:11:51.708 --> 00:11:53.903
a series
of sub-harmonic pulses.

00:11:53.944 --> 00:11:55.002
They stand the best chance

00:11:55.045 --> 00:11:56.478
of transmission
through the wormhole.

00:11:56.513 --> 00:11:57.480
Acknowledged.

00:11:57.514 --> 00:11:58.481
Proceed.

00:11:58.515 --> 00:11:59.709
Aye, Captain.

00:11:59.750 --> 00:12:02.412
I'm reading transmission
of the test signal.

00:12:02.452 --> 00:12:04.943
The probe has received it
and relayed it.

00:12:04.988 --> 00:12:07.650
How will we know
if the signal reaches somebody?

00:12:07.691 --> 00:12:09.090
The only way...

00:12:09.126 --> 00:12:11.754
is if that somebody answers.

00:12:26.376 --> 00:12:27.900
There's no response.

00:12:27.944 --> 00:12:29.673
It's too soon.

00:12:29.713 --> 00:12:30.975
Remember, we have no idea

00:12:31.014 --> 00:12:33.346
how long it takes
to reach the other side.

00:12:33.383 --> 00:12:35.374
Are you reading anything,
Mr. Tuvok?

00:12:35.419 --> 00:12:36.579
Negative, Captain.

00:12:36.620 --> 00:12:39.521
There is nothing that
would suggest a response.

00:12:39.556 --> 00:12:41.547
Even if someone
receives our signal,

00:12:41.591 --> 00:12:43.991
it might take them some time
to figure out how to return it.

00:12:44.027 --> 00:12:46.393
You're right.
Janeway to Kim.

00:12:46.430 --> 00:12:47.829
Continue transmitting.

00:12:47.864 --> 00:12:48.956
Aye, Captain.

00:12:48.999 --> 00:12:50.864
How long should we keep it up?

00:12:50.901 --> 00:12:52.732
Until I tell you otherwise.

00:12:52.769 --> 00:12:54.600
You have the Bridge, Commander.

00:12:54.638 --> 00:12:56.765
Captain.

00:12:56.807 --> 00:12:58.638
Mr. Tuvok.

00:12:58.675 --> 00:13:00.006
I'm getting something, Captain.

00:13:00.110 --> 00:13:01.441
I'm getting it, too.

00:13:01.478 --> 00:13:03.946
A subspace signal relayed
through the probe.

00:13:04.047 --> 00:13:05.412
That signal is
being transmitted

00:13:05.449 --> 00:13:08.543
at exactly the same frequency
and amplitude as our signal.

00:13:08.585 --> 00:13:10.052
It's a response.

00:13:10.087 --> 00:13:12.647
Someone received
our transmission,

00:13:12.689 --> 00:13:14.953
and sent one back.

00:13:15.025 --> 00:13:18.119
And their signal
originated in the...

00:13:18.161 --> 00:13:20.095
Alpha Quadrant.

00:13:29.339 --> 00:13:31.432
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:13:31.475 --> 00:13:32.942
Encouraged by his success

00:13:32.976 --> 00:13:35.444
in transmitting a signal
to the Alpha Quadrant,

00:13:35.479 --> 00:13:37.674
Mr. Kim is investigating
the possibility

00:13:37.714 --> 00:13:38.908
of establishing a voice link

00:13:38.949 --> 00:13:41.941
with whoever is at
the other end of the wormhole.

00:13:47.424 --> 00:13:48.721
Come in.

00:13:50.694 --> 00:13:53.754
Kes, this is a surprise.

00:13:53.797 --> 00:13:55.355
Am I interrupting?

00:13:55.399 --> 00:13:56.491
Not at all.

00:13:56.533 --> 00:13:58.433
I was just going to have
a cup of soup.

00:13:58.468 --> 00:13:59.730
Would you like anything?

00:13:59.770 --> 00:14:01.635
Uh, spinach juice
with a touch of pear, please.

00:14:01.672 --> 00:14:02.832
Tom Paris
introduced me to it.

00:14:02.873 --> 00:14:03.862
It's very nutritious.

00:14:03.907 --> 00:14:05.033
I'm sure.

00:14:05.075 --> 00:14:07.373
Computer, one spinach juice
with a touch of pear,

00:14:07.411 --> 00:14:09.174
and one cup
of vegetable bouillon.

00:14:18.488 --> 00:14:20.046
What can I do for you?

00:14:24.428 --> 00:14:27.158
If there were
a member of the crew

00:14:27.197 --> 00:14:30.963
whose needs weren't being met,
would you want to know about it?

00:14:31.068 --> 00:14:32.501
Of course.

00:14:32.536 --> 00:14:35.664
Kes, do you and Neelix feel

00:14:35.706 --> 00:14:37.105
that your needs
are being ignored?

00:14:37.140 --> 00:14:38.129
Of course not.

00:14:38.175 --> 00:14:39.665
We're very happy here.

00:14:39.710 --> 00:14:42.736
I'm referring to the Doctor.

00:14:42.779 --> 00:14:43.973
The Doctor?

00:14:44.081 --> 00:14:45.309
I don't understand

00:14:45.348 --> 00:14:47.077
why people treat him
the way they do.

00:14:50.353 --> 00:14:51.911
How do people treat him?

00:14:51.955 --> 00:14:53.354
As though he doesn't exist.

00:14:53.390 --> 00:14:56.223
They talk about him
while he's standing right there.

00:14:56.259 --> 00:14:59.490
They ignore him,
they insult him.

00:14:59.529 --> 00:15:01.622
Well, as a matter of fact,

00:15:01.665 --> 00:15:03.860
I've been hearing the
other side of the coin.

00:15:03.900 --> 00:15:05.424
Many of the crew
have complained

00:15:05.469 --> 00:15:07.369
that the Doctor is
brusque, even rude...

00:15:07.404 --> 00:15:09.167
that he lacks
any bedside manner.

00:15:09.206 --> 00:15:11.674
We've been talking
about reprogramming him.

00:15:11.708 --> 00:15:13.232
You can do that?

00:15:13.276 --> 00:15:14.903
It doesn't seem right.

00:15:14.945 --> 00:15:17.311
Kes, he's only a hologram.

00:15:17.347 --> 00:15:19.838
He's your Medical Officer.
He's alive.

00:15:19.883 --> 00:15:21.407
No, he's not.

00:15:21.451 --> 00:15:24.420
He's self-aware.
He's communicative.

00:15:24.454 --> 00:15:26.615
He has the ability to learn.

00:15:26.656 --> 00:15:29.090
Because he's been programmed
to do that.

00:15:29.126 --> 00:15:30.957
So because he's a hologram,

00:15:31.061 --> 00:15:34.758
he doesn't have to be treated
with respect,

00:15:34.798 --> 00:15:37.266
or any consideration at all?

00:15:40.370 --> 00:15:42.133
Very well.

00:15:42.172 --> 00:15:43.867
I'll look into it.

00:15:43.907 --> 00:15:45.374
Thank you, Captain.

00:15:53.617 --> 00:15:56.586
Okay, we'll be ready to go
on line in a couple minutes.

00:15:56.620 --> 00:15:58.986
I'm still worried about the
gravitational interference.

00:15:59.022 --> 00:16:00.990
I don't think
the covariant isolator

00:16:01.024 --> 00:16:02.855
will be effective
with a vocal transmission.

00:16:02.893 --> 00:16:05.418
Let's try inverting
the narrow band filter.

00:16:09.099 --> 00:16:10.191
Progress report, Ensign.

00:16:10.233 --> 00:16:12.098
I think we're ready
to give it a try,

00:16:12.135 --> 00:16:13.227
but we're pushing through

00:16:13.270 --> 00:16:15.238
some pretty heavy
gravitational interference.

00:16:15.272 --> 00:16:17.433
I can't guarantee the clarity
of the transmission.

00:16:17.474 --> 00:16:19.874
Let's see what happens.

00:16:19.910 --> 00:16:21.571
This is Captain Kathryn Janeway

00:16:21.611 --> 00:16:23.943
of the Federation
Starship Voyager.

00:16:23.980 --> 00:16:25.413
Do you read?

00:16:27.851 --> 00:16:30.684
I'll narrow the filter band-pass
some more.

00:16:30.720 --> 00:16:32.210
Try again, Captain.

00:16:32.255 --> 00:16:35.952
This is Kathryn Janeway
of the Federation Ship Voyager.

00:16:36.026 --> 00:16:40.053
Is anyone receiving
this communication?

00:16:41.798 --> 00:16:43.993
...vessel...

00:16:45.669 --> 00:16:47.762
Narrow the band-pass
a little more.

00:16:49.105 --> 00:16:50.572
Try again, Captain.

00:16:50.607 --> 00:16:52.165
This is Janeway.

00:16:52.209 --> 00:16:54.200
Please repeat
your last transmission.

00:16:56.613 --> 00:16:58.979
...cargo vessel...

00:17:00.917 --> 00:17:02.817
...Quadrant...

00:17:02.853 --> 00:17:04.718
...your location.

00:17:04.754 --> 00:17:06.654
Cargo vessel, we're still trying

00:17:06.690 --> 00:17:08.385
to clear up
your last transmission.

00:17:08.425 --> 00:17:10.791
Please repeat one more time.

00:17:10.827 --> 00:17:13.421
I am Captain
of the Cargo Vessel Talvath.

00:17:13.463 --> 00:17:18.230
Location Alpha Quadrant,
sector 1385.

00:17:18.268 --> 00:17:19.599
What is your location?

00:17:19.636 --> 00:17:21.729
We are in the Delta Quadrant,

00:17:21.771 --> 00:17:23.864
but since this Quadrant
hasn't been charted,

00:17:23.907 --> 00:17:26.307
I can't specify
our exact location.

00:17:26.343 --> 00:17:28.334
Please confirm.

00:17:28.378 --> 00:17:29.811
You said Delta Quadrant?

00:17:29.846 --> 00:17:31.711
Correct.

00:17:31.748 --> 00:17:33.545
In a Federation starship?

00:17:33.583 --> 00:17:35.312
Yes. We were on a mission

00:17:35.352 --> 00:17:37.843
and we got pulled
into this Quadrant.

00:17:37.888 --> 00:17:38.946
Pulled in? How?

00:17:38.989 --> 00:17:40.456
It's a complicated story.

00:17:40.490 --> 00:17:42.549
Please, if you would just
try deconstructing

00:17:42.592 --> 00:17:44.355
the phase shift
of our hailing frequency,

00:17:44.394 --> 00:17:46.157
you can verify.

00:17:46.196 --> 00:17:48.756
You are undoubtedly
still in the Alpha Quadrant.

00:17:48.798 --> 00:17:50.129
What are your coordinates?

00:17:50.166 --> 00:17:52.225
I assure you
I am telling you the truth.

00:17:52.269 --> 00:17:57.206
We are in the Delta Quadrant,
70,000 light-years from you.

00:17:57.240 --> 00:17:58.400
This is preposterous.

00:17:58.441 --> 00:17:59.738
You are obviously lying.

00:17:59.776 --> 00:18:01.471
I am terminating communication.

00:18:01.511 --> 00:18:02.808
No. No, wait.

00:18:02.846 --> 00:18:04.973
Kim, hail him again.

00:18:06.149 --> 00:18:07.741
No response, Captain.

00:18:10.520 --> 00:18:12.613
Why would he have
broken off transmission?

00:18:14.791 --> 00:18:16.782
Perhaps I can offer
an explanation.

00:18:16.826 --> 00:18:20.023
The com-link signature
of his transmission indicates

00:18:20.063 --> 00:18:22.429
the message originated
from a Romulan ship.

00:18:22.465 --> 00:18:24.899
Further, there are
no known shipping lanes

00:18:24.935 --> 00:18:27.028
in the sector he identified.

00:18:27.070 --> 00:18:29.538
Given the precise calibration
of his signal,

00:18:29.572 --> 00:18:33.064
I would suggest that he is in
fact on board a science vessel.

00:18:33.109 --> 00:18:35.168
Why would he pretend
to be a cargo captain?

00:18:35.211 --> 00:18:37.736
If he's engaged in some
kind of secret research,

00:18:37.781 --> 00:18:38.941
he might want
to conceal that fact.

00:18:39.049 --> 00:18:40.846
Precisely.

00:18:40.884 --> 00:18:42.476
And when we claimed
to be transmitting

00:18:42.519 --> 00:18:43.747
from the Delta Quadrant...

00:18:43.787 --> 00:18:45.482
an impossibility
so far as he knows...

00:18:45.522 --> 00:18:47.888
he may have feared
we were Federation spies.

00:18:47.924 --> 00:18:48.891
Just our luck.

00:18:48.925 --> 00:18:50.392
We raise one ship
from the Alpha Quadrant

00:18:50.427 --> 00:18:51.860
and it has to be Romulan.

00:18:51.895 --> 00:18:53.954
That Romulan
still has the ability

00:18:54.030 --> 00:18:55.930
to get a message to Starfleet.

00:18:55.966 --> 00:18:59.060
Mr. Kim, hail the Talvath
repeatedly.

00:18:59.102 --> 00:19:01.161
Call me the minute
you reestablish contact.

00:19:01.204 --> 00:19:02.899
Commander, you have the Bridge.

00:19:02.973 --> 00:19:04.099
Aye, Captain.

00:19:19.956 --> 00:19:23.858
Computer, initiate emergency
medical holographic program.

00:19:23.893 --> 00:19:26.726
Please state the nature
of the medical emergency.

00:19:26.763 --> 00:19:29.197
There is no emergency, Doctor.

00:19:29.232 --> 00:19:32.497
Well... that's good.

00:19:32.535 --> 00:19:34.400
I was right in the middle
of preparing a culture

00:19:34.437 --> 00:19:36.200
to test Lieutenant Hargrove
for Arethian flu

00:19:36.239 --> 00:19:38.366
when Ensign Kyoto
deactivated me.

00:19:38.408 --> 00:19:41.343
I'm sure she didn't realize
you were busy.

00:19:41.378 --> 00:19:43.403
What is it you wanted, Captain?

00:19:43.446 --> 00:19:46.938
Actually, I thought
we might just...

00:19:47.050 --> 00:19:49.348
talk for a moment.

00:19:49.386 --> 00:19:50.410
About what?

00:19:50.453 --> 00:19:53.513
Doctor, you were
originally programmed

00:19:53.556 --> 00:19:56.423
to serve in a limited fashion
during an emergency.

00:19:56.459 --> 00:19:58.552
Now you're being asked
to do much more.

00:19:59.729 --> 00:20:01.594
That's certainly true.

00:20:01.631 --> 00:20:03.360
I'm providing full-time
medical service

00:20:03.400 --> 00:20:04.890
for the entire ship's crew,

00:20:04.934 --> 00:20:06.959
functioning as both
doctor and nurse

00:20:07.070 --> 00:20:08.901
and now as an instructor
as well.

00:20:08.938 --> 00:20:11.270
You don't have the luxury
of thinking of yourself

00:20:11.307 --> 00:20:13.798
as an emergency
medical program anymore.

00:20:13.843 --> 00:20:17.176
You've become a full-fledged
member of the crew.

00:20:17.213 --> 00:20:19.875
I see.

00:20:19.916 --> 00:20:22.384
Are you suggesting
that I be reprogrammed?

00:20:22.419 --> 00:20:24.410
No.

00:20:25.822 --> 00:20:28.916
I'm asking if there's
anything I can do...

00:20:28.958 --> 00:20:30.949
to help you.

00:20:30.994 --> 00:20:32.325
Help me?

00:20:32.362 --> 00:20:35.331
If there's anything
you need or want,

00:20:35.365 --> 00:20:37.299
I'd like to see that you get it.

00:20:37.333 --> 00:20:40.393
What I'd like is to be turned
off when people leave.

00:20:40.437 --> 00:20:44.203
I spend hours here with
absolutely nothing to do.

00:20:44.240 --> 00:20:46.538
When someone does remember
to deactivate me,

00:20:46.576 --> 00:20:48.806
they do so without asking
if it's convenient.

00:20:48.845 --> 00:20:51.040
It's extremely irritating.

00:20:53.316 --> 00:20:56.342
What if I gave you control...

00:20:58.755 --> 00:21:01.383
over your deactivation sequence?

00:21:01.424 --> 00:21:03.551
I beg your pardon?

00:21:03.593 --> 00:21:06.357
I'm sure we can make it possible
for you to turn yourself off,

00:21:06.396 --> 00:21:08.387
or to prevent being turned off.

00:21:08.431 --> 00:21:12.390
I... I might like that.

00:21:12.435 --> 00:21:15.370
I'll have someone look into it.

00:21:17.307 --> 00:21:19.332
Anything else?

00:21:19.375 --> 00:21:21.707
I'm not sure.

00:21:21.744 --> 00:21:23.473
I'll have to give it
some thought.

00:21:25.448 --> 00:21:27.040
You do that.

00:21:50.073 --> 00:21:52.405
Kim to Captain Janeway.

00:21:52.442 --> 00:21:54.501
Janeway here.

00:21:54.544 --> 00:21:57.604
Captain, we've got him back...
the Romulan.

00:21:57.647 --> 00:22:00.013
Good work.

00:22:00.116 --> 00:22:01.913
Put him through to my quarters.

00:22:06.188 --> 00:22:08.122
This is Kathryn Janeway.

00:22:08.157 --> 00:22:11.320
This is the Cargo Vessel
Talvath.

00:22:11.360 --> 00:22:13.920
Thank you for answering
our hail, Captain.

00:22:13.963 --> 00:22:16.431
What is your name?

00:22:16.465 --> 00:22:17.932
How may I address you?

00:22:22.571 --> 00:22:25.199
I'd prefer not to give my name.

00:22:25.241 --> 00:22:26.970
Very well.

00:22:27.076 --> 00:22:29.237
I understand that you
must have been skeptical

00:22:29.278 --> 00:22:30.711
when I told you where we are.

00:22:30.746 --> 00:22:33.579
I hope you've been able
to verify our position.

00:22:33.616 --> 00:22:37.643
My analysis of your hailing
frequency seems to indicate

00:22:37.686 --> 00:22:40.246
that it originates
in the Delta Quadrant,

00:22:40.289 --> 00:22:42.086
but I am not precluding
the possibility

00:22:42.124 --> 00:22:45.582
that you've been able to create
that illusion somehow.

00:22:45.628 --> 00:22:47.994
To what end?

00:22:48.063 --> 00:22:51.965
I'm not sure, but that doesn't
negate the possibility.

00:22:54.036 --> 00:22:57.096
How can I assure you
of my truthfulness?

00:22:57.139 --> 00:22:59.801
You say
you are a Federation ship.

00:22:59.842 --> 00:23:01.810
Are you a Starfleet vessel?

00:23:04.713 --> 00:23:06.772
Yes, we are.

00:23:06.815 --> 00:23:09.648
And your mission
in the Delta Quadrant?

00:23:09.685 --> 00:23:13.746
Our mission was originally
in the Alpha Quadrant.

00:23:13.789 --> 00:23:16.883
We were pulled against our will
to our present location.

00:23:16.925 --> 00:23:20.224
Now we're trying to get home.

00:23:20.262 --> 00:23:22.662
Aren't you in fact
Starfleet spies

00:23:22.698 --> 00:23:24.632
on a surveillance mission?

00:23:24.667 --> 00:23:29.104
Captain, I understand
your concern.

00:23:29.138 --> 00:23:31.971
Naturally, the Romulan Empire

00:23:32.007 --> 00:23:35.534
doesn't want Starfleet
spying on its science vessels,

00:23:35.577 --> 00:23:40.139
but since we're 70,000
light-years from Romulan space,

00:23:40.182 --> 00:23:43.242
and a subspace message
to Starfleet would take years,

00:23:43.285 --> 00:23:44.980
I think you have to admit

00:23:45.087 --> 00:23:48.716
that we can't be much
of a threat to you.

00:23:48.757 --> 00:23:52.488
You have nothing
to fear from us.

00:23:52.528 --> 00:23:54.120
Soothing words, Captain,

00:23:54.163 --> 00:23:56.597
but they are only words.

00:23:59.568 --> 00:24:02.036
If we were spies,

00:24:02.071 --> 00:24:06.337
we wouldn't be asking
what I'm going to ask you now.

00:24:09.511 --> 00:24:12.378
We have no way of communicating
with Starfleet...

00:24:12.414 --> 00:24:14.541
with our friends and families.

00:24:19.655 --> 00:24:23.591
We're hoping you might be able
to relay a message for us.

00:24:25.761 --> 00:24:27.956
Our crew is not large.

00:24:28.030 --> 00:24:31.227
Each of them could write
a short, personal message.

00:24:31.266 --> 00:24:35.066
You'd be welcome to read them
all before passing them on.

00:24:35.104 --> 00:24:37.698
And I think you'd be convinced
that they're nothing more

00:24:37.740 --> 00:24:40.800
than the heartfelt words
of some...

00:24:40.843 --> 00:24:43.243
very lonely people.

00:24:46.014 --> 00:24:49.882
Captain...
it would ease my apprehension

00:24:49.918 --> 00:24:52.751
if I could see that you are
who you say you are.

00:24:52.788 --> 00:24:56.155
I have a signal amplifier
on board.

00:24:56.191 --> 00:24:58.625
I've been working
to reconfigure the protocols

00:24:58.660 --> 00:25:01.754
to penetrate the radiation
stream of the wormhole.

00:25:01.797 --> 00:25:03.924
I think it might be possible

00:25:03.999 --> 00:25:06.695
to establish
a visual link between us.

00:25:06.735 --> 00:25:09.067
I have no objection.

00:25:10.539 --> 00:25:12.734
When that's done...

00:25:12.775 --> 00:25:15.300
will you help us?

00:25:15.344 --> 00:25:17.175
I make no promises.

00:25:17.212 --> 00:25:20.340
Let us proceed
one step at a time.

00:25:20.382 --> 00:25:21.940
Have your officers contact me

00:25:21.984 --> 00:25:23.918
in order to attempt
the visual link.

00:25:23.952 --> 00:25:28.048
- Good night.
- Good night.

00:25:44.573 --> 00:25:46.803
We're ready to try a visual link
with the Romulan ship, Captain.

00:25:46.842 --> 00:25:47.968
Good work.

00:25:48.010 --> 00:25:50.808
We didn't have any trouble
configuring the protocols.

00:25:50.846 --> 00:25:52.746
But that phase variance
in the radiation stream

00:25:52.781 --> 00:25:53.839
gave us a few problems.

00:25:53.882 --> 00:25:55.645
Torres is going
to balance it manually

00:25:55.684 --> 00:25:56.776
from Engineering.

00:25:56.819 --> 00:25:57.979
Okay.

00:25:58.086 --> 00:26:00.213
We've got the communications
frequency locked in.

00:26:01.723 --> 00:26:03.213
On screen.

00:26:17.239 --> 00:26:18.934
I presume
you are Captain Janeway.

00:26:19.041 --> 00:26:20.668
Yes.

00:26:20.709 --> 00:26:25.840
I want to thank you, Captain,
for maintaining contact with us.

00:26:25.881 --> 00:26:28.816
It means a great deal
to me and to my crew.

00:26:30.752 --> 00:26:33.721
I am not familiar
with this class of ship.

00:26:33.755 --> 00:26:35.780
It's new,
but it isn't classified.

00:26:37.159 --> 00:26:39.093
I'm a little surprised
your intelligence

00:26:39.127 --> 00:26:40.958
hasn't provided you
with information.

00:26:40.996 --> 00:26:43.726
I've been at space
for over a year, Captain,

00:26:43.765 --> 00:26:45.699
and am not privy
to the latest intelligence.

00:26:45.734 --> 00:26:48.862
I'm sure that our operatives
have provided the government

00:26:48.904 --> 00:26:51.702
with detailed information
about your new ship.

00:26:51.740 --> 00:26:53.105
No doubt.

00:26:53.141 --> 00:26:56.110
Captain, have you been able

00:26:56.144 --> 00:26:57.372
to communicate
with your government

00:26:57.412 --> 00:26:59.243
about sending our messages?

00:26:59.281 --> 00:27:01.476
I have.

00:27:01.517 --> 00:27:04.486
They've promised to take
the matter under advisement.

00:27:04.520 --> 00:27:06.385
I see.

00:27:06.421 --> 00:27:09.151
And when do you think
they will have an answer?

00:27:09.191 --> 00:27:11.489
It is impossible
to predict the timetable

00:27:11.527 --> 00:27:12.858
of the Romulan Senate.

00:27:12.895 --> 00:27:15.329
When they've made their
decision, I will hear from them.

00:27:15.364 --> 00:27:18.333
We don't have the luxury
of a great deal of time.

00:27:18.367 --> 00:27:21.427
My officers are predicting that
the probe will become inoperable

00:27:21.470 --> 00:27:23.028
in the next 48 hours.

00:27:23.071 --> 00:27:25.699
Captain, I am
a low-ranking scientist,

00:27:25.741 --> 00:27:27.208
a minor functionary.

00:27:27.242 --> 00:27:30.473
It is not my place
to tell the Romulan Senate

00:27:30.512 --> 00:27:32.946
to speed up their
decision-making process.

00:27:32.981 --> 00:27:36.678
You said you've been in space
for over a year.

00:27:39.187 --> 00:27:40.916
Do you have any family?

00:27:45.160 --> 00:27:46.525
Yes.

00:27:46.562 --> 00:27:48.894
I assume they're not with you
in space.

00:27:50.699 --> 00:27:56.501
My wife... and my daughter
are on Romulus.

00:27:56.538 --> 00:27:58.472
A daughter...

00:27:58.507 --> 00:28:00.031
How old is she?

00:28:01.877 --> 00:28:06.371
She is... seven months.

00:28:08.183 --> 00:28:09.741
Then you've never seen her.

00:28:11.053 --> 00:28:12.884
To my sorrow, no.

00:28:12.921 --> 00:28:16.448
She'll be two years old
before I get back.

00:28:16.491 --> 00:28:18.891
You must miss your family
very much.

00:28:20.996 --> 00:28:23.590
I knew when I accepted
this assignment

00:28:23.632 --> 00:28:25.930
that there would be
a price to pay.

00:28:26.034 --> 00:28:31.028
Perhaps I didn't realize
how high that price would be.

00:28:31.073 --> 00:28:33.268
Captain...

00:28:33.308 --> 00:28:38.940
every one of us on this ship
has left behind friends, family,

00:28:38.981 --> 00:28:40.346
loved ones.

00:28:40.382 --> 00:28:43.180
We may not see them again
for years...

00:28:43.218 --> 00:28:44.480
maybe never.

00:28:44.519 --> 00:28:48.512
So we can all understand
how lonely you must be.

00:28:48.557 --> 00:28:52.857
Surely you can understand
our feelings as well.

00:28:52.894 --> 00:28:56.625
We would be deeply grateful
for any efforts you might make

00:28:56.665 --> 00:28:59.759
to persuade your government
to send our messages.

00:29:04.272 --> 00:29:08.868
I cannot guarantee success,
but I will try to persuade

00:29:08.910 --> 00:29:13.176
my superiors to make
their decision quickly...

00:29:15.317 --> 00:29:16.579
and positively.

00:29:16.618 --> 00:29:18.586
Thank you.

00:29:20.422 --> 00:29:22.185
I will contact you again.

00:29:27.229 --> 00:29:31.290
Commander, let's assume
he's going to be successful.

00:29:31.333 --> 00:29:33.597
Tell the crew
to prepare personal messages

00:29:33.635 --> 00:29:35.569
and have them ready
within the hour.

00:29:35.604 --> 00:29:37.469
With pleasure, Captain.

00:29:42.444 --> 00:29:43.809
Captain, I have to talk to you.

00:29:43.845 --> 00:29:45.608
Go ahead, Torres.

00:29:45.647 --> 00:29:47.979
No!
I mean, in private.

00:29:55.424 --> 00:29:56.721
I think this will work, Captain,

00:29:56.758 --> 00:29:57.816
but I didn't want
to bring it up

00:29:57.859 --> 00:29:58.848
in front of the crew.

00:29:58.894 --> 00:30:00.521
It wouldn't be right
to get their hopes up

00:30:00.562 --> 00:30:02.553
in case it doesn't work,
although I think it will.

00:30:02.598 --> 00:30:03.565
Slow down, Torres,

00:30:03.599 --> 00:30:06.159
and tell me
what you're talking about.

00:30:06.201 --> 00:30:08.601
The phase amplitude

00:30:08.637 --> 00:30:10.969
of the visual link
with the Romulan ship...

00:30:11.039 --> 00:30:13.098
it's within just a few megahertz

00:30:13.141 --> 00:30:15.473
of meeting
transporter protocols.

00:30:17.045 --> 00:30:17.977
Are you suggesting?

00:30:18.046 --> 00:30:18.978
We might be able

00:30:19.047 --> 00:30:20.674
to piggy-back
a transporter beam

00:30:20.716 --> 00:30:21.944
onto the visual link.

00:30:21.984 --> 00:30:24.885
We could transport the entire
crew back to the Alpha Quadrant.

00:30:24.920 --> 00:30:27.650
You'll have to reconfigure
the matter transmission rate...

00:30:27.689 --> 00:30:28.781
Fairly substantially.

00:30:28.824 --> 00:30:30.485
...and we risk losing
whatever we try to beam out.

00:30:30.525 --> 00:30:32.823
We'll have to run
a series of tests first.

00:30:32.861 --> 00:30:34.192
See to it, Lieutenant.

00:30:34.229 --> 00:30:35.253
I'll need some help.

00:30:35.297 --> 00:30:37.265
You have my authorization
to use any

00:30:37.299 --> 00:30:38.698
of the ship's personnel
you need.

00:30:38.734 --> 00:30:39.701
This is top priority.

00:30:39.735 --> 00:30:41.168
And don't worry about secrecy.

00:30:41.203 --> 00:30:43.763
I doubt you'll be able to keep
this quiet for very long.

00:31:09.898 --> 00:31:11.832
I finished these,
and I'm ready for more.

00:31:11.867 --> 00:31:13.494
You finished those already?

00:31:13.535 --> 00:31:15.526
I enjoyed studying anatomy.

00:31:15.570 --> 00:31:18.471
It would be interesting
to see an autopsy sometime.

00:31:20.642 --> 00:31:22.576
What are the bones
of the middle ear?

00:31:22.611 --> 00:31:24.738
Malleus, incus and stapes.

00:31:24.780 --> 00:31:25.804
And the connective tissue

00:31:25.847 --> 00:31:28.247
between the middle
and the external auditory canal?

00:31:28.283 --> 00:31:29.978
The tympanic membrane.

00:31:30.018 --> 00:31:33.078
Hmm. I suspect you have
an eidetic memory...

00:31:33.121 --> 00:31:34.418
an astonishing gift.

00:31:34.456 --> 00:31:37.152
I'll do a full neural scan
on you at some point.

00:31:37.192 --> 00:31:39.990
I've been thinking...

00:31:40.062 --> 00:31:42.530
if we do get back
to Federation space,

00:31:42.564 --> 00:31:43.997
I'd like to explore
the possibility

00:31:44.099 --> 00:31:45.726
of going to medical school.

00:31:45.767 --> 00:31:48.463
If you continue to apply
yourself as you have,

00:31:48.503 --> 00:31:50.528
by the time we get back,
you may already have

00:31:50.572 --> 00:31:52.164
the equivalent
of a medical degree.

00:31:52.207 --> 00:31:53.299
Then you haven't heard?

00:31:53.341 --> 00:31:54.330
Heard what?

00:31:54.376 --> 00:31:56.901
That we might
be getting back soon.

00:31:58.547 --> 00:32:00.913
If there's one thing
you can count on,

00:32:00.949 --> 00:32:02.314
it's that I am the last
to be told

00:32:02.350 --> 00:32:03.942
about anything that happens
on this ship.

00:32:04.052 --> 00:32:06.077
Everyone's talking about it.

00:32:06.121 --> 00:32:08.783
There may be a way
to transport all of us

00:32:08.824 --> 00:32:09.950
to the Alpha Quadrant.

00:32:10.025 --> 00:32:12.084
Chief Torres
and half of Engineering

00:32:12.127 --> 00:32:13.754
are working on it right now.

00:32:14.930 --> 00:32:16.454
I see.

00:32:16.498 --> 00:32:18.227
Well, I'll say good-bye now.

00:32:18.266 --> 00:32:20.496
I won't be transporting
with the rest of you.

00:32:20.535 --> 00:32:22.969
But can't we download your
program and take you with us?

00:32:23.038 --> 00:32:26.337
My program is fully integrated
into the Sick Bay system.

00:32:26.374 --> 00:32:29.343
At present, I...
cannot be downloaded.

00:32:36.284 --> 00:32:38.275
Thank you for everything.

00:32:40.188 --> 00:32:41.450
Wait. I'd like...

00:32:42.924 --> 00:32:44.414
That is...

00:32:44.459 --> 00:32:46.723
could I ask a favor of you?

00:32:46.762 --> 00:32:48.593
Anything.

00:32:48.630 --> 00:32:51.531
If you do leave, before you go,

00:32:51.566 --> 00:32:55.502
would you check to make sure
I've been deactivated?

00:32:55.537 --> 00:32:57.471
I promise.

00:33:07.149 --> 00:33:08.173
And our Chief Engineer

00:33:08.216 --> 00:33:09.945
has managed to bind
a transporter beam

00:33:10.051 --> 00:33:11.916
to the visual link between us.

00:33:11.953 --> 00:33:14.080
Then you've matched
your data transmission

00:33:14.122 --> 00:33:16.386
to the phase amplitude
of our com signal?

00:33:16.424 --> 00:33:17.891
Exactly.

00:33:17.926 --> 00:33:21.157
Apparently,
our intelligence operatives

00:33:21.196 --> 00:33:22.925
are not doing their job.

00:33:22.964 --> 00:33:26.195
You clearly have technology
that we are unaware of.

00:33:26.234 --> 00:33:28.566
This would be
an incredible breakthrough

00:33:28.603 --> 00:33:30.366
in subspace field mechanics.

00:33:30.405 --> 00:33:33.306
If it's successful,
we'd like to try transmitting

00:33:33.341 --> 00:33:34.365
a test cylinder to you.

00:33:34.409 --> 00:33:37.469
A test cylinder of what sort?

00:33:37.512 --> 00:33:39.537
It is a standard
Starfleet mechanism

00:33:39.581 --> 00:33:41.446
with a varietal
molecular matrix.

00:33:41.483 --> 00:33:43.951
It simulates most known organic
and non-organic compounds.

00:33:43.985 --> 00:33:46.579
It is not classified technology.

00:33:46.621 --> 00:33:48.816
Ah, I am aware
of this mechanism.

00:33:48.857 --> 00:33:50.518
We use a similar device.

00:33:50.559 --> 00:33:52.789
I will allow the transport.

00:33:52.828 --> 00:33:55.695
Bridge to Transporter Room 1.

00:33:55.730 --> 00:33:56.697
Torres here.

00:33:56.731 --> 00:33:58.426
We're all set, Captain.

00:33:58.466 --> 00:33:59.956
The lock is active,

00:34:00.001 --> 00:34:01.730
and we're focused
on the Romulan's

00:34:01.770 --> 00:34:02.930
transporter coordinates.

00:34:02.971 --> 00:34:04.097
All right, then.

00:34:07.475 --> 00:34:09.033
Let's give it a try.

00:34:09.077 --> 00:34:10.840
Energize.

00:34:16.384 --> 00:34:18.682
The cylinder
has dematerialized, Captain.

00:34:25.327 --> 00:34:26.794
Can you get it back?

00:34:26.828 --> 00:34:27.886
The pattern buffer

00:34:27.929 --> 00:34:29.954
is having trouble accepting
the matter stream.

00:34:29.998 --> 00:34:32.694
I'll increase power
to the phase transition coils.

00:34:41.843 --> 00:34:43.970
Ramp the coils to 37 megajoules.

00:34:44.045 --> 00:34:45.478
37 megajoules.

00:35:01.930 --> 00:35:05.093
Congratulations, Captain.
You've done it.

00:35:05.133 --> 00:35:07.328
Very impressive.

00:35:07.369 --> 00:35:10.031
We should run a series of these
tests, just to make sure,

00:35:10.071 --> 00:35:12.369
but we have to act quickly
before the probe is crushed.

00:35:12.407 --> 00:35:14.136
I understand.

00:35:14.175 --> 00:35:17.076
Eventually, we'll have to try
transporting a person.

00:35:17.112 --> 00:35:19.546
One of our crew
will beam to your ship,

00:35:19.581 --> 00:35:20.639
if you'll allow it.

00:35:20.682 --> 00:35:22.445
I'm afraid
I can't permit that, Captain.

00:35:22.484 --> 00:35:23.883
My government would never allow

00:35:23.919 --> 00:35:26.080
Starfleet personnel
on this ship.

00:35:26.121 --> 00:35:29.090
I wouldn't want my logs
to show that activity.

00:35:29.124 --> 00:35:31.183
Then what would you suggest?

00:35:31.226 --> 00:35:36.823
I'll volunteer to transport
to your ship... and back again.

00:35:36.865 --> 00:35:38.332
But, Captain...

00:35:38.366 --> 00:35:41.767
if we can't transport
to your ship,

00:35:41.803 --> 00:35:43.737
how are we to get back?

00:35:46.341 --> 00:35:48.366
If the procedure is successful,

00:35:48.410 --> 00:35:51.174
I'll arrange for a troop ship
to join me.

00:35:51.212 --> 00:35:53.442
That would easily
accommodate your crew.

00:35:53.481 --> 00:35:54.971
Very well.

00:35:55.050 --> 00:35:56.210
We'll be in touch.

00:36:09.730 --> 00:36:10.924
Kim and Torres have made

00:36:10.998 --> 00:36:13.330
more than 20 transports
of the test cylinder.

00:36:13.367 --> 00:36:14.834
Even though
she's still having trouble

00:36:14.868 --> 00:36:15.892
with that phase variance,

00:36:15.936 --> 00:36:17.369
every one of them
has been successful.

00:36:17.404 --> 00:36:19.304
Let's hope it goes as well
with the Romulan.

00:36:19.340 --> 00:36:20.932
Captain, I must insist
I stay with him

00:36:20.975 --> 00:36:22.567
at all times
while he is on board.

00:36:22.610 --> 00:36:23.599
Agreed.

00:36:23.644 --> 00:36:24.804
We're locked on to him.

00:36:24.845 --> 00:36:26.437
Whenever you're ready, Captain.

00:36:26.480 --> 00:36:29.847
Well, let's try it.

00:36:29.883 --> 00:36:31.316
Energize.

00:36:40.327 --> 00:36:41.453
What's the problem?

00:36:41.495 --> 00:36:43.895
It's the phase variance
in the radiation stream.

00:36:43.931 --> 00:36:45.990
I'm balancing it manually.

00:36:57.177 --> 00:37:01.978
Welcome to the Delta Quadrant...
Captain.

00:37:15.963 --> 00:37:18.488
My First Officer,
Commander Chakotay.

00:37:18.532 --> 00:37:20.523
Lieutenant Tuvok,
Head of Security.

00:37:20.567 --> 00:37:21.829
Chief Engineer Torres...

00:37:21.869 --> 00:37:25.066
and Operations Officer Kim.

00:37:27.508 --> 00:37:30.807
My congratulations on your
remarkable accomplishment.

00:37:30.844 --> 00:37:34.439
This is an astonishing
breakthrough.

00:37:34.481 --> 00:37:35.573
For a while there,
I didn't think

00:37:35.616 --> 00:37:36.583
you were going to make it.

00:37:36.617 --> 00:37:38.482
There was a strange
phase variance

00:37:38.519 --> 00:37:39.918
in the radiation stream.

00:37:39.953 --> 00:37:42.080
It almost kept us from
pulling you through.

00:37:42.122 --> 00:37:46.252
Mr. Tuvok, you may begin
evacuation procedures.

00:37:46.293 --> 00:37:48.659
I suggest we delay that
for the moment, Captain.

00:37:48.696 --> 00:37:52.860
I'm afraid I found the reason
for the unusual phase variance.

00:37:52.900 --> 00:37:54.458
What is it?

00:37:54.501 --> 00:37:56.992
Captain, what year is it?

00:37:59.039 --> 00:38:00.267
What year?

00:38:00.307 --> 00:38:01.604
If you please.

00:38:03.711 --> 00:38:06.737
By your calendar,
the year is 2351.

00:38:09.717 --> 00:38:13.585
But... this is 2371.

00:38:13.620 --> 00:38:15.053
Exactly.

00:38:15.089 --> 00:38:18.456
Our Romulan visitor is
a person out of time.

00:38:18.492 --> 00:38:21.586
He's showing clear evidence
of temporal displacement.

00:38:21.628 --> 00:38:25.758
I would surmise
that the wormhole is a rift

00:38:25.799 --> 00:38:28.563
not just in space, but in time.

00:38:28.602 --> 00:38:30.365
The unusual phase variance
we detected

00:38:30.404 --> 00:38:33.862
was actually an indication
of a temporal shift.

00:38:34.975 --> 00:38:38.467
We have transported him
from 20 years in the past

00:38:38.512 --> 00:38:39.911
to our present.

00:38:45.252 --> 00:38:47.652
I've gone over and over
the transporter logs.

00:38:47.688 --> 00:38:49.553
There is no question
that if we try

00:38:49.590 --> 00:38:52.081
to transport ourselves
through that wormhole,

00:38:52.126 --> 00:38:54.754
we'll end up 20 years
in the past.

00:38:54.795 --> 00:38:57.525
Then let's do it.

00:38:57.564 --> 00:39:00.829
It's better than spending
the next 70 years

00:39:00.868 --> 00:39:01.835
trying to get back.

00:39:01.869 --> 00:39:03.268
How can we do that?

00:39:03.303 --> 00:39:04.531
We'd be going back to a time

00:39:04.571 --> 00:39:06.038
when you were
only two years old.

00:39:06.073 --> 00:39:08.906
I know you're
disappointed, Harry.

00:39:09.009 --> 00:39:10.704
We all are.

00:39:10.744 --> 00:39:14.305
It seemed we were so close...

00:39:16.517 --> 00:39:19.645
but clearly, we can't go back.

00:39:19.686 --> 00:39:23.247
It would pollute the timeline
to such an extent

00:39:23.290 --> 00:39:25.383
that the consequences
would be unimaginable.

00:39:25.426 --> 00:39:29.920
I'm afraid we'll have
to send you back alone,

00:39:30.030 --> 00:39:31.691
and ask that you
not reveal anything

00:39:31.732 --> 00:39:33.131
that has happened here.

00:39:33.167 --> 00:39:36.159
I can assure you, Captain,
that I would not do anything

00:39:36.203 --> 00:39:38.933
that might contaminate
the future and perhaps harm

00:39:38.972 --> 00:39:40.769
the Romulan Empire.

00:39:42.609 --> 00:39:43.735
But...

00:39:45.112 --> 00:39:47.273
in 20 years...

00:39:49.516 --> 00:39:52.508
I could alert Starfleet
not to launch

00:39:52.553 --> 00:39:54.544
the mission
which sent you here.

00:39:54.588 --> 00:39:58.046
I'm afraid
that's not possible either.

00:39:59.293 --> 00:40:01.090
We've already had a huge impact
on this Quadrant.

00:40:01.128 --> 00:40:04.529
People and events here
would be drastically affected.

00:40:09.369 --> 00:40:12.497
I'm afraid we're left
with our original request.

00:40:17.177 --> 00:40:18.804
In 20 years...

00:40:18.846 --> 00:40:22.145
would you relay our personal
messages to Starfleet?

00:40:22.182 --> 00:40:23.843
Of course.

00:40:23.884 --> 00:40:27.251
At the proper time,
I will transmit them.

00:40:31.124 --> 00:40:34.685
If you should find a way back
within my lifetime...

00:40:37.097 --> 00:40:38.758
I'd be an old man,

00:40:38.799 --> 00:40:42.132
but I would welcome
a message from you.

00:40:42.169 --> 00:40:47.038
I am Telek R'Mor of the Romulan
Astrophysical Academy.

00:40:50.911 --> 00:40:53.277
I promise you'll hear from us...

00:40:55.782 --> 00:40:57.579
because we will get back.

00:41:01.622 --> 00:41:03.886
These are our messages.

00:41:06.260 --> 00:41:08.820
I wish you luck on your journey.

00:41:08.862 --> 00:41:11.558
And I thank you for your help.

00:41:23.043 --> 00:41:24.704
Energize.

00:41:38.258 --> 00:41:39.953
His signal's
in the pattern buffer.

00:41:39.993 --> 00:41:42.154
Transferring
to the emitter array.

00:41:42.195 --> 00:41:43.856
Phase variance is
out of sync again.

00:41:43.897 --> 00:41:45.330
Compensating.

00:41:48.869 --> 00:41:51.394
Transport complete, Captain.

00:41:51.438 --> 00:41:53.429
He made it.

00:41:56.877 --> 00:41:59.573
I'll tell the crew.

00:41:59.613 --> 00:42:00.910
They can have the satisfaction

00:42:00.948 --> 00:42:03.508
of knowing that their messages
have reached their families.

00:42:03.550 --> 00:42:05.518
Captain.

00:42:06.720 --> 00:42:09.780
I did not want to mention this
until after our guest had left.

00:42:09.823 --> 00:42:11.290
I checked
the computer's data banks

00:42:11.325 --> 00:42:13.953
for a Romulan scientist
named Telek R'Mor.

00:42:14.027 --> 00:42:15.961
And?

00:42:16.029 --> 00:42:17.963
I'm sorry to report

00:42:18.065 --> 00:42:20.795
Dr. R'Mor died in 2367.

00:42:21.802 --> 00:42:23.963
That was four years ago.

00:42:24.004 --> 00:42:25.767
That is correct.

00:42:25.806 --> 00:42:28.434
Before he would have sent
our messages.

00:42:35.449 --> 00:42:36.973
Maybe he left a will,

00:42:37.084 --> 00:42:39.575
telling someone else
to transmit the messages

00:42:39.620 --> 00:42:42.111
or he could have given
our computer chip

00:42:42.155 --> 00:42:43.315
to the Romulan government.

00:42:43.357 --> 00:42:45.291
It is possible.

00:42:45.325 --> 00:42:47.759
Unfortunately,
there is no way to know.

00:42:55.636 --> 00:42:57.661
Then let's move on.

00:42:57.704 --> 00:43:00.468
We've got a long way to go.

00:43:12.719 --> 00:43:14.710
I tried
a new hamstring exercise...

00:43:14.755 --> 00:43:16.484
maybe I overdid it...

00:43:16.523 --> 00:43:18.889
but my workouts are about
all that stand between me

00:43:18.925 --> 00:43:20.688
and a severe case
of cabin fever.

00:43:22.462 --> 00:43:25.727
Lieutenant, I am the Chief
Medical Officer of this ship.

00:43:25.766 --> 00:43:26.960
If you have something
to say to me,

00:43:27.067 --> 00:43:29.968
please direct
the statement to me.

00:43:30.070 --> 00:43:31.799
Well...

00:43:33.306 --> 00:43:36.469
you see, I need to work out.

00:43:36.510 --> 00:43:37.977
I'm not telling you
not to work out.

00:43:38.011 --> 00:43:39.376
I'm suggesting

00:43:39.413 --> 00:43:42.075
you use a modicum of common
sense when you do it.

00:43:42.115 --> 00:43:45.084
If I see you in here again
for an exercise-related injury,

00:43:45.118 --> 00:43:47.848
I'll have to discuss the matter
with your superior officer.

00:43:47.888 --> 00:43:49.788
Yes... sir.

00:43:49.823 --> 00:43:51.552
You're fine now.
You may leave.

00:43:51.591 --> 00:43:52.615
Yes, sir.

00:43:53.894 --> 00:43:55.452
Thank you, sir.

00:44:00.734 --> 00:44:01.928
I don't think
he'll make the mistake

00:44:02.002 --> 00:44:03.697
of ignoring you again.

00:44:04.938 --> 00:44:07.532
Captain Janeway has made me
realize that I must function

00:44:07.574 --> 00:44:09.872
as more than an emergency
medical replacement.

00:44:09.910 --> 00:44:13.903
I must think of myself
as a... member of the crew.

00:44:13.947 --> 00:44:16.245
You're absolutely right.

00:44:17.718 --> 00:44:18.776
I've prepared a list

00:44:18.819 --> 00:44:21.754
of things I'd like to see
added to Sick Bay.

00:44:21.788 --> 00:44:25.815
Perhaps you could
present it to the Captain?

00:44:25.859 --> 00:44:27.451
I'd be happy to.

00:44:28.495 --> 00:44:31.259
There's one more request...

00:44:31.298 --> 00:44:34.859
something of a...
a personal nature.

00:44:36.303 --> 00:44:38.669
I would like...

00:44:38.705 --> 00:44:40.172
a name.
